---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Before & After Studio Privacy Policy"
  description="How Before & After Studio handles local photos and projects, Google Play purchases, SDK technical data, sharing and deletion."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Before & After Studio</p>
    <h1>
      Privacy Policy — <em>Before &amp; After Studio</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Effective date:</strong> November 6, 2026
      <br />
      <strong>Developer:</strong> Velvet &amp; Pixel
      <br />
      <strong>Contact:</strong>{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Before &amp; After Studio is a photo comparison and editing application.
      Photos are edited locally on your Android device. No Velvet &amp; Pixel
      account is required, and we do not operate a server that receives or
      stores your photos, projects, logos, or editing history.
    </p>
    <h2>Photos and projects</h2>
    <p>
      Photos and logos you select are imported into the application&#x27;s
      private local storage. Editing, alignment, rendering, saved projects,
      thumbnails, and branding presets are handled on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Imported originals may retain metadata, including location information.
      The app&#x27;s generated JPEG and PNG exports do not intentionally copy
      the original photos&#x27; location metadata. The original source images
      are not modified.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app uses Android&#x27;s system photo picker, with a system document
      picker fallback where needed. It does not request unrestricted access to
      your photo library. A photo or document provider you choose may offer
      cloud features under its own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <h2>Google Play purchases and local purchase records</h2>
    <p>
      Before &amp; After Studio offers an optional one-time Pro purchase through
      Google Play Billing. Google processes payment using your Google Play
      account. The app does not receive or store your payment card details.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app receives purchase information from Google Play, including signed
      purchase proof and purchase tokens, to verify ownership and unlock Pro.
      Purchase proof and the free-export allowance are stored privately on your
      device, separately from projects and excluded from backup. The app
      verifies signed purchase proof locally and acknowledges purchases through
      Google Play; Velvet &amp; Pixel does not operate a purchase-verification
      server.
    </p>
    <p>
      Previously verified Pro access is cached for offline use. Purchases,
      restoration, product prices and online ownership checks use Google Play. A
      successful ownership refresh can remove refunded or revoked access.
      Clearing app storage or uninstalling removes the local records but does
      not cancel or erase a completed Google Play purchase. Eligible purchases
      can be restored using the purchasing Google account for this app.
    </p>
    <h2>Google SDK technical data and network access</h2>
    <p>
      The app includes Google Play Billing and related Google SDKs. In addition
      to purchase processing, these SDKs send operational and diagnostic
      information to Google. This can include the app package and version,
      Billing SDK and Android versions, device manufacturer/model/build
      information, language and country settings, network and carrier
      information, event timing, billing operation results, error codes and
      diagnostic messages, and temporary billing-session identifiers.
    </p>
    <p>
      These services can run when the app starts and when checking Google Play
      connectivity, prices or purchase ownership, as well as during checkout and
      restoration. Technical processing is not limited to users who choose to
      purchase Pro. The app does not pass your photos, logos, projects or
      finished comparisons to the billing SDK.
    </p>
    <p>
      SDK diagnostic events may be queued locally for later transmission. The
      Google diagnostic uploader used by the included DataTransport library is
      configured with an HTTPS endpoint. Google determines how it handles and
      retains information on its services under its own policies. Deleting
      projects, clearing app storage or uninstalling does not delete information
      already held by Google.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google may also process information needed for payment processing,
      verification, fraud prevention and operation of Google Play. See
      Google&#x27;s Privacy Policy, Google Play Terms of Service, and
      Google&#x27;s information about data retention and privacy controls. We do
      not promise a fixed deletion period for Google-held information.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
          Google’s Privacy Policy
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/">
          Google Play Terms of Service
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention">
          Google data retention information
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy">
          Google Account data and privacy controls
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Advertising and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The app does not include developer-operated advertising, analytics or
      crash-reporting services. Google SDK operational diagnostics are described
      above. The app has no ads or subscriptions.
    </p>
    <h2>Sharing and exporting</h2>
    <p>
      You control when and where you save or share exported images. When you
      choose a destination through Android sharing or save to a cloud-connected
      destination, that application or service may process the image under its
      own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Exported images, shared copies, and original source photos outside the app
      are not removed when a project is deleted or the app is uninstalled.
      Delete those copies separately from their respective locations.
    </p>
    <h2>Storage, retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Projects, imported photos and logos, presets, thumbnails, and
      purchase-related local records are retained on your device while needed
      for the app or until you remove them. App-managed project and purchase
      storage is excluded from Android cloud backup and device transfer. The app
      does not provide its own cloud backup or project synchronization.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting a project removes that project. Imported assets still referenced
      by another project or branding preset are retained. Cleanup of
      unreferenced assets is best effort and may be retried when the app starts.
      Deleting a project does not reset the local free-export allowance or
      remove a Pro purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clearing the app&#x27;s storage in Android Settings or uninstalling
      removes its private local data, including projects and the local
      free-export allowance. Export any finished images you want to keep first.
      Google-held payment and technical records are governed by Google&#x27;s
      policies and controls, rather than the app&#x27;s project-delete action.
    </p>
    <h2>Children&#x27;s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Before &amp; After Studio is a general-purpose creative tool and is not
      specifically designed for children. We do not knowingly operate a service
      that collects children&#x27;s personal information.
    </p>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses Android&#x27;s application-private storage and
      system-provided mechanisms for selecting photos, saving and sharing.
      Private storage is access control; the app does not add a separate
      encryption layer to its project or purchase-record files. Digital
      signatures on purchase proof verify authenticity rather than encrypting
      its contents. Google&#x27;s services have their own security practices. No
      software can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the app&#x27;s functionality, integrations,
      or legal requirements change. The updated effective date will appear on
      this page.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
